{% comment %}
  Alt text, resolved in one place.

  Every image on the site was reaching the page with `alt=""` unless someone had
  typed alt text into the Shopify admin for that specific image — which, for a
  bulk-imported pharmacy catalogue, is essentially never. A product image with an
  empty alt is announced by a screen reader as nothing at all, so a collection
  grid read as a list of prices with no products attached.

  ORDER OF PRECEDENCE — the first rule that applies wins:

    1. Whatever a person wrote in the admin. Manual alt text always survives;
       this snippet only ever fills a gap, it never overwrites. That is the whole
       reason the fallback lives here rather than being hardcoded at each call
       site — one place to be sure of the precedence.
    2. Product title, plus the variant name when the image belongs to a specific
       variant. "Sudocrem Antiseptic Healing Cream — 250g" tells you which of the
       five tins you are looking at; "Sudocrem Antiseptic Healing Cream" five
       times does not.
    3. Collection title, for category and banner imagery.
    4. Empty, for decoration. An empty alt is correct for a decorative image and
       is not the same thing as a missing one: it tells assistive tech to skip
       the image rather than to guess at it from the filename.

  Deliberately NOT done here: describing what is in the picture. That is
  copywriting, it needs a human who can see the image, and a wrong description is
  worse than a plain one. This gives every image an accurate, mechanical name.

  Usage:
    {%- capture alt -%}{%- render 'image-alt', image: img, product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {{ img | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag: alt: alt }}

  Accepts:
    image      — the image or media object; its own .alt wins if set
    product    — for rule 2
    variant    — optional; overrides the variant lookup when the caller knows it
    collection — for rule 3
    decorative — pass true to force an empty alt regardless of everything above
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign manual = image.alt | default: '' | strip

  if decorative
    # nothing: a decorative image takes an empty alt, and says so deliberately.
  elsif manual != blank
    echo manual
  else
    assign variant_name = ''

    # A caller that already knows the variant is trusted over the lookup.
    if variant and variant.title != 'Default Title'
      assign variant_name = variant.title
    elsif image.attached_to_variant? and image.variants.size > 0
      assign first_variant = image.variants | first
      if first_variant.title != 'Default Title'
        assign variant_name = first_variant.title
      endif
    endif

    if product and product.title != blank
      if variant_name != blank
        echo product.title | append: ' — ' | append: variant_name
      else
        echo product.title
      endif
    elsif collection and collection.title != blank
      echo collection.title
    endif
  endif
-%}
